-- Served a day late.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), did I apply in time to restore the appeal` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both well before the last day.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), did I apply in time to restore the appeal` (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 3 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The absent party applied, in time, and shows good reason.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), may the Court restore the appeal for rehearing` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No good reason shown: "must show good reason".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), may the Court restore the appeal for rehearing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not filed and served in time.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), may the Court restore the appeal for rehearing` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The application is not by the absent party.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 8(3), may the Court restore the appeal for rehearing` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 9 -- expedited appeal =====
-- The appeal is urgent.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 9(1), may the Court order an expedited appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not urgent, but there is a special reason.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 9(1), may the Court order an expedited appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither: the "if" is not met.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 9(1), may the Court order an expedited appeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An expedited appeal: the Court may dispense with or modify provisions.
