-- Not all the parties consent.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(2), must the security for costs be paid out and the undertaking discharged on withdrawal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- There are outstanding issues: any party may ask for directions.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(3), may I ask the appellate Court in writing for directions on the outstanding issues` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No outstanding issues: the "if" is not met.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(3), may I ask the appellate Court in writing for directions on the outstanding issues` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Court has not directed otherwise: "no oral arguments are to be made".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(3), may I make oral arguments in my request for directions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Court has directed otherwise: what it allows is not in the Rules.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(3), may I make oral arguments in my request for directions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outstanding issues and the Registrar has not removed it: it remains on the list.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(4), does my appeal or application stay on the list while issues are outstanding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Registrar has removed it under paragraph (3): "Except as provided".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(4), does my appeal or application stay on the list while issues are outstanding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No outstanding issues: the "if" is not met.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 10(4), does my appeal or application stay on the list while issues are outstanding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

