#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(2), must I be told who decided the matter, what was decided and when, where it was decided without oral arguments` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The date was not given.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(2), must I be told who decided the matter, what was decided and when, where it was decided without oral arguments` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Oral arguments were heard: paragraph (2) is for a matter decided without them.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(2), must I be told who decided the matter, what was decided and when, where it was decided without oral arguments` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In writing and the charges are paid.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(3), am I entitled to a copy of the decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Charges not paid: "upon payment".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(3), am I entitled to a copy of the decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not given in writing: paragraph (3) speaks only of a decision given in writing.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(3), am I entitled to a copy of the decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Delivered orally by a Judge who heard the appeal.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(4), may the judgment be delivered orally although another Judge who heard the appeal is absent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not so delivered: paragraph (4) speaks only of oral delivery by a Judge sitting in the Court.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 12(4), may the judgment be delivered orally although another Judge who heard the appeal is absent` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ===== Division 2 -- Appeal from the District Court and the Magistrate's Court to the General Division (rules 13 to 23) =====
-- Running example: a judgment of the District Court dated 27 January 2026.  Fourteen days after it, counted under Order 3, rule 3, is 10 February 2026.

-- ===== Rule 13 -- scope of this Division =====
-- A trial of an originating claim in the District Court, appealed to the General Division: paragraph (1)(a).
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `District Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` `Originating claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Damages assessed by a District Judge in the Magistrate's Court: paragraph (1)(b).
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `Magistrate's Court` `A Magistrate` `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken` `Originating claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A committal order for contempt in the Magistrate's Court: paragraph (1)(c).
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `Magistrate's Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court` `Originating application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A trial of an originating application is not named: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `District Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` `Originating application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Damages assessed by someone other than a District Judge: not named.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `District Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken` `Originating claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An application for a prerogative order: not named.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `District Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(d) an application for a prerogative order` `Originating claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A judgment of the General Division: not within this Division.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `General Division` `A Judge` `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` `Originating claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An appeal that is not to the General Division: not within this Division.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(1), does Division 2 apply to my appeal against a judgment of the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` `District Court` `A District Judge` `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` `Originating claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The District Court, against whose judgment an appeal is brought: the "lower Court".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(2), is this court the "lower Court"` `District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Magistrate's Court likewise.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(2), is this court the "lower Court"` `Magistrate's Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No appeal brought or being brought against its judgment.
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(2), is this court the "lower Court"` `District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The General Division is not the District Court or Magistrate's Court: "means".
#ASSERT `Under Order 19, rule 13(2), is this court the "lower Court"` `General Division` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

