-- ============================================================
-- roc5: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- CASES for the seat layer roc5-seat.l4 (Orders 20 to 22).  Each question is asked through the seat with plain inputs
-- ("I answer yes / no / I am not sure" for a fact from another part), and the answer must be the one the layer-1 rule
-- gives on the same facts.  The expected values are those of the layer-1 test files, which were written from the text of
-- the Rules before the modules were run; here they are asked from the seat.  Every question has at least one case, and
-- every question that can say "not covered" has a case that does.  Scenario cases written for the seat end the file.


§ `Cases -- Order 20`

-- Order 20, rule 1
