§ `Scenarios -- facts a party would state, asked in the order a party meets them`

-- Scenario 1.  I am appealing a tribunal's decision under a statute that provides for the appeal.
-- The decision was given on 1 January 2027, so (counting under Order 3, Rule 3) the 14 days end on 15 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 1, does Order 20 apply to my proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` TRUE FALSE `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 3(1), have I brought my appeal or application in the way the rule requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my originating application and affidavit in time` (Date 15 1 2027) (Date 15 1 2027) (Date 15 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my originating application and affidavit in time` (Date 15 1 2027) (Date 16 1 2027) (Date 15 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Filed on 15 January 2027: the case conference must be within 6 weeks, that is by 26 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 4(1), did the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer yes` (Date 26 2 2027) (Date 26 2 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 4(1), did the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer yes` (Date 27 2 2027) (Date 26 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The hearing is on 1 April 2027, so written submissions are due at least 14 days before, that is by 18 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 5(1), did I file and serve my written submissions in time` (Date 18 3 2027) (Date 18 3 2027) (Date 18 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 5(1), did I file and serve my written submissions in time` (Date 18 3 2027) (Date 19 3 2027) (Date 18 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 5(2), are my written submissions within the page limit` 35 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 5(2), are my written submissions within the page limit` 36 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Nothing in a written law or in an order stays enforcement of the tribunal's decision: the appeal does not operate as a stay.
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 6, does my appeal or application operate as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The proceeding is of a kind Order 20 does not name: the Rules do not answer.
#ASSERT `Under Order 20, rule 1, does Order 20 apply to my proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1) another kind of proceeding` TRUE FALSE `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer no` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Scenario 2.  I won my action and want my costs.  The matter was finally disposed of on 1 June 2027, so the bill of costs is due by 1 June 2028.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 3(2), must the Court order the costs in my favour as the successful party` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 3(2), must the Court order the costs in my favour as the successful party` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 17, did I file my bill of costs in time` (Date 1 6 2028) (Date 1 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 17, did I file my bill of costs in time` (Date 2 6 2028) (Date 1 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Registrar decided an item on 10 November 2027; the review application may be made within 14 days after, that is by 24 November 2027.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 27(2), did I apply for review in time` (Date 24 11 2027) (Date 24 11 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 27(2), did I apply for review in time` (Date 25 11 2027) (Date 24 11 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Registrar is not a Judge for the review: Rule 27(5) says what "Judge" means and the Registrar is not in it.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 27(5), is a person a Judge in Rules 27 and 28` `o 21 r 27(5) the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Court has ordered my costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis: they are assessed on that basis.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 22(1), are the costs assessed on the indemnity basis` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The assessed costs are 10,000 dollars: the interest for one year at 5.33% per year is 533 dollars.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 29(1), what is the interest on the costs for one year` `o 21 r 29(1)(a) assessed costs` 10000 EQUALS JUST 533
-- I was a trustee in the proceedings and the Court has said nothing different: I may take my costs out of the fund.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 3(5), am I entitled to my costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property` `o 21 r 3(5) trustee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The capacity in which I acted is not one the rule names: the Rules do not answer.
#ASSERT `Under Order 21, rule 3(5), am I entitled to my costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property` `o 21 r 3(5) another capacity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Scenario 3.  I hold a judgment and have an enforcement order issued on 1 March 2027; 12 months beginning with that date end on 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 2(5), is the enforcement order valid in the first instance on this day` (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 2(5), is the enforcement order valid in the first instance on this day` (Date 1 3 2028) (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am a non-party served on 1 July 2027 with a notice of attachment; no notice of objection is filed.
-- 21 days after service end on 22 July 2027, and I must pay over within 7 days after that, that is by 29 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 6(10), as a non-party, did I hand or pay over the money and the commission in time` FALSE (Date 29 7 2027) (Date 29 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 6(10), as a non-party, did I hand or pay over the money and the commission in time` FALSE (Date 30 7 2027) (Date 29 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- If a notice of objection was filed, the rule's "if no notice of objection is filed" fails, so the answer is no (a failed "if" counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29); rule 10 then governs.
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 6(10), as a non-party, did I hand or pay over the money and the commission in time` TRUE (Date 30 7 2027) (Date 29 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Sheriff's commission on money attached: 2%, at least $100 and at most $50,000.
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 9(2), what is the Sheriff's commission` `o 22 r 9(2)(a) the gross amount of deposits, money or debt attached` 100000 EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 9(2), what is the Sheriff's commission` `o 22 r 9(2)(a) the gross amount of deposits, money or debt attached` 100 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 9(2), what is the Sheriff's commission` `o 22 r 9(2)(a) the gross amount of deposits, money or debt attached` 5000000 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 9(2), what is the Sheriff's commission` `o 22 r 9(2) another amount` 100000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A Court order provides for payment by instalments and none is due yet: the Rules do not say whether I may apply; once one is due and unpaid, I may.
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 12, may the enforcement applicant apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Order 22, rule 12, may the enforcement applicant apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

