-- ============================================================
-- Cases for roc6-seat.l4: every question in the seat layer, with the facts a real party would state.
-- Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, before the code was run.
-- A "last day" is the last day of the period as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it; the days used here are made up.


§ `Cases -- Order 23 -- Contempt of court (committal)`

#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an affidavit that sets out (a), (b) and (c)
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- (b), the committal respondent's details, missing: the Rule is silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- (a), the committal applicant's details, missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no affidavit
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 4(1), did I apply for the committal order within 14 days after the Court gave permission` TRUE (Date 14 1 2026) (Date 14 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 4(1), did I apply for the committal order within 14 days after the Court gave permission` TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 14 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- one day late
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 4(1), did I apply for the committal order within 14 days after the Court gave permission` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 14 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no permission yet: "After permission is granted" has not happened
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 4(2), is there at least 21 days between serving the committal respondent and the hearing date` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 4(2), is there at least 21 days between serving the committal respondent and the hearing date` (Date 6 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- served too late
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 7(3), may I, as the committal applicant, rely on this ground at the hearing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a ground in the affidavit
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 7(3), may I, as the committal applicant, rely on this ground at the hearing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only the grounds set out in the affidavit"
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 8(3), may I apply for the suspension of the committal order to be lifted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a term was broken
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 8(3), may I apply for the suspension of the committal order to be lifted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the Rule gives the ground only
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 11(1), is my committal order in the form the Rules require` "Form 42" EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Form 42
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 11(1), is my committal order in the form the Rules require` "Form 41" EQUALS NOTHING -- another form: the Rule is silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 15(4), has the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapsed` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served one day late: it lapses
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 15(4), has the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapsed` TRUE (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- served on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 15(4), has the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapsed` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- never served and the 14 days have run
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 16(2), did I apply in time to vary or set aside the non-publication direction` TRUE (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 16(2), did I apply in time to vary or set aside the non-publication direction` TRUE (Date 15 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- late
#ASSERT `Under Order 23, rule 16(2), did I apply in time to vary or set aside the non-publication direction` FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under section 13(9)

