#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 2, what is the value of my claim for court fees in the Supreme Court, in dollars` TRUE 50000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 50000 -- a liquidated demand
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 2, what is the value of my claim for court fees in the Supreme Court, in dollars` TRUE 50000 TRUE 30000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 80000 -- liquidated and unliquidated, the aggregate
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 2, what is the value of my claim for court fees in the Supreme Court, in dollars` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1000000 -- none of the listed kinds: up to $1 million, answered as 1000000 (assumed, see NOTES.md)
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(3)(a), is my request for refund of hearing fees made in writing in time` TRUE (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(3)(a), is my request for refund of hearing fees made in writing in time` TRUE (Date 15 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- late
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(3)(a), is my request for refund of hearing fees made in writing in time` FALSE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- in time but not in writing
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(4), must the Court refund the whole of the hearing fees I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 5 2026) (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- notified on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(4), must the Court refund the whole of the hearing fees I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 11 5 2026) (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a day too late
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(5), may I ask a Judge by letter to review the Registrar's decision` TRUE TRUE (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 3(5), may I ask a Judge by letter to review the Registrar's decision` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- late
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 4(2)(b), is my application for refund of the fee for an unused document in time` (Date 12 8 2026) (Date 12 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 4(2)(b), is my application for refund of the fee for an unused document in time` (Date 13 8 2026) (Date 12 8 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- late
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 5, is the hearing in my proceeding one for which no hearing fee is payable` `o 25 r 5(a) an action for damages for death or personal injuries` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an action for damages for death or personal injuries
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 5, is the hearing in my proceeding one for which no hearing fee is payable` `o 25 r 5 some other proceeding` EQUALS NOTHING -- the Rule does not say a fee is payable for another proceeding
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 6, is a hearing fee payable in my winding up proceedings` `o 25 r 6 a company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a company, special hearing dates
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 6, is a hearing fee payable in my winding up proceedings` `o 25 r 6 a company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither limb
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 6, is a hearing fee payable in my winding up proceedings` `o 25 r 6 some other entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another entity
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 7(1), may the Registrar issue me a certificate of exemption from fees and security for costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- satisfied and applied for
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 7(1), may the Registrar issue me a certificate of exemption from fees and security for costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Registrar is not satisfied
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 7(1), may the Registrar issue me a certificate of exemption from fees and security for costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- satisfied, but you are not that party or have not applied
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` `District Court` TRUE TRUE `o 25 r 8(3) some other action` `roc6 No` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an ordinary action in a District Court, such as a contract claim: the fee is payable under paragraph (1)
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` `District Court` TRUE TRUE `o 25 r 8(3)(a) a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` `roc6 Yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a non-injury motor accident action: paragraph (3)(a)
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` `District Court` TRUE TRUE `o 25 r 8(3)(a) a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` `roc6 I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING -- whether it is a non-injury motor accident action is for Order 21
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` `District Court` TRUE TRUE `o 25 r 8(3)(b) an action for damages for death or personal injuries` `roc6 No` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no Court ADR fee in a death or personal injuries action
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` `General Division` TRUE TRUE `o 25 r 8(3)(b) an action for damages for death or personal injuries` `roc6 No` EQUALS NOTHING -- not a District Court case
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(4), is my request for refund of the Court ADR fee made in writing to the Registrar in time` TRUE (Date 14 12 2026) (Date 14 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 25, rule 8(4), is my request for refund of the Court ADR fee made in writing to the Registrar in time` TRUE (Date 15 12 2026) (Date 14 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- late

§ `Cases -- Order 26 -- Registry and administration`

#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 3(4), may the Registrar allow me to search for, inspect and take a copy of a document filed in Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- valid interest and the fee
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 3(4), may the Registrar allow me to search for, inspect and take a copy of a document filed in Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no fee
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 3(7), is the document I want to file in the form the Rules require` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- both
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 3(7), is the document I want to file in the form the Rules require` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not typewritten and printed: the Rule is silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 5(1), must the Registry be open on this day` (Date 7 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an ordinary Friday
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 5(1), must the Registry be open on this day` (Date 8 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a Saturday
#ASSERT `Under Order 26, rule 5(1), must the Registry be open on this day` (Date 10 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a public holiday

§ `Cases -- Order 27 -- Lodgment in Court, money in Registry and payment to Sheriff`

#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 2(1), have I, as a trustee, applied to pay money into Court in the way the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a full affidavit
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 2(1), have I, as a trustee, applied to pay money into Court in the way the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no affidavit needed for such a legacy
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 2(1), have I, as a trustee, applied to pay money into Court in the way the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the affidavit lacks the description of the trust
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 3, have I given the notice of lodgment the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- lodged and gave notice
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 3, have I given the notice of lodgment the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "must forthwith give notice": silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 3, have I given the notice of lodgment the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- did not lodge
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 4(1), am I lodging money in Court by the form the Rule requires` "Form 44(a)" EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Form 44(a)
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 4(1), am I lodging money in Court by the form the Rule requires` "Form 44(b)" EQUALS NOTHING -- another form: silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest` 30000 `roc6 No` `roc6 No` `roc6 No` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- $30,000 exactly, none of the exceptions
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest` 29999 `roc6 No` `roc6 No` `roc6 No` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- less than $30,000
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest` 100000 `roc6 No` `roc6 No` `roc6 No` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- security for costs
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest` 100000 `roc6 I am not sure` `roc6 No` `roc6 No` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not sure whether Order 9, Rule 17 applies
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 17, have I produced a copy of the judgment or order and given notice to the person entitled` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- both
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 17, have I produced a copy of the judgment or order and given notice to the person entitled` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice: silent on what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 27, rule 17, have I produced a copy of the judgment or order and given notice to the person entitled` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no payment under a judgment or order

-- ============================================================
-- roc7: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Orders 28 to 33: CASES for the seat layer (roc7-seat).
-- One or more cases for every seat question, with the facts a party would state.  Each expected value is the one written beside
-- the layer-1 assertion the case is lifted from (written from the text of the rule, never copied from what the code printed).
-- A case that expects NOTHING is a case the Rules do not cover.  The "last day" in a case is the date Order 3, Rule 3 would
-- give, stated as a plain date.


-- Order 28 -- Electronic filing service

-- Order 28, rule 1: Definitions of this Order
-- Order 28, rule 1: am I an authorised user of the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, am I an authorised user of the electronic filing service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 1 “authorised user”: every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, am I an authorised user of the electronic filing service` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 1 “authorised user”: condition 1 missing
-- Order 28, rule 1: is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 1 “registered user”: every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 1 “registered user”: condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 1 “registered user”: condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 1: is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service` `o 28 r 1 sole proprietorship` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a sole proprietorship
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service` `o 28 r 1 law corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a law corporation
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service` `o 28 r 1 the Attorney-General's Chambers` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Attorney-General's Chambers
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service` `o 28 r 1 any other kind of body` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in the closed list
-- Order 28, rule 1: is a deeming under Order 28 still standing in my favour?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is a deeming under Order 28 still standing in my favour` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the contrary is not proved
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 1, is a deeming under Order 28 still standing in my favour` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the contrary is proved: the deeming ends

-- Order 28, rule 6: Registered user and authorised user
-- Order 28, rule 6(1): may I, as an entity, apply to be a registered user?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(1), may I, as an entity, apply to be a registered user` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 6(1): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(1), may I, as an entity, apply to be a registered user` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(1): condition 1 missing
-- Order 28, rule 6(2): may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(2), may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 6(2): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(2), may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(2): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(2), may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(2): condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 6(5): am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 6(5): every condition met, the contrary not proved
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 6(5): deemed until the contrary is proved (O 28 r 1), and it has been
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(5): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(5): condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 6(6): have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(6), have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 6(6): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(6), have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(6): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 6(6), have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 6(6): condition 2 missing

-- Order 28, rule 7: Fee for registered user
-- Order 28, rule 7(1): is the fee payable by me as a registered user?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), is the fee payable by me as a registered user` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- not a service bureau
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), is the fee payable by me as a registered user` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a service bureau: taken out of the class (QE default)
-- Order 28, rule 7(1): what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- no band describes 0
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 1 EQUALS JUST 25 -- (a) a single advocate and solicitor: $25
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 2 EQUALS JUST 35 -- (b) 2 to 5: $35
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 6 EQUALS JUST 70 -- (c) 6 to 9: $70
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 10 EQUALS JUST 140 -- (d) 10 to 19: $140
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 20 EQUALS JUST 250 -- (e) 20 to 49: $250
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 50 EQUALS JUST 500 -- (f) 50 to 99: $500
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 100 EQUALS JUST 1000 -- (g) 100 to 199: $1,000
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` 200 EQUALS JUST 2000 -- (h) 200 or more: $2,000
-- Order 28, rule 7(1): what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month` 1 3 EQUALS JUST 75 -- $25 a month for 3 months or parts of a month
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month` 7 2 EQUALS JUST 140 -- $70 a month for 2 months
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month` 0 3 EQUALS NOTHING -- no band
-- Order 28, rule 7(2)(c): what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect` 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- no authorised user designated: no band describes 0
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect` 1 EQUALS JUST 25 -- one authorised user counts as a single advocate and solicitor: $25
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect` 6 EQUALS JUST 70 -- six authorised users: the 6 to 9 band, $70
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect` 200 EQUALS JUST 2000 -- 200 authorised users: the top band, $2,000
-- Order 28, rule 7(3): is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(3), is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 7(3): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(3), is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 7(3): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(3), is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 7(3): condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 7(6): on what day is the fee for a month due and payable?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(6), on what day is the fee for a month due and payable` 2026 3 EQUALS Date 1 3 2026 -- the first day of the month
-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a): does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` TRUE TRUE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paid in error, claimed in writing on 10 March, within the 3 months
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` TRUE TRUE 2026 6 15 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the claim came the day after the 3 months ran out: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- no claim made yet and the 3 months are still running: the Rules do not yet answer
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` TRUE FALSE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no claim in writing: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` FALSE TRUE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- nothing was paid in excess or error
-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a): has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` TRUE TRUE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the duty arose and the Registrar refunded
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` TRUE TRUE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the duty arose and no refund yet: a bare must, the Rules do not say what follows
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` TRUE TRUE 2026 6 15 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the claim was late, so the duty did not arise
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` FALSE TRUE 2026 3 10 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- nothing was paid in excess or error, so no duty arose
-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a): did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` 2026 6 13 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim: done before the last day
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` 2026 6 14 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim: done on the last day (boundary)
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` 2026 6 15 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim: done the day after the last day (boundary)
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` 0 0 0 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim: not yet done, period still running
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` 0 0 0 (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim: not done and the period has run out

-- Order 28, rule 8: Electronic filing
-- Order 28, rule 8(1): am I required to use the electronic filing service for this document?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), am I required to use the electronic filing service for this document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(1) arises: every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), am I required to use the electronic filing service for this document` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 8(1) arises: condition 1 missing
-- Order 28, rule 8(1): have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(1): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(1): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(1): condition 2 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(1): condition 3 missing
-- Order 28, rule 8(2): is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(2), is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(2): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(2), is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(2): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(2), is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(2): condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 8(3): is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(3), is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- by electronic transmission
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(3), is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- via a service bureau
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(3), is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither
-- Order 28, rule 8(4): may a document be filed other than using the electronic filing service?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(4), may a document be filed other than using the electronic filing service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(4): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(4), may a document be filed other than using the electronic filing service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(4): condition 1 missing
-- Order 28, rule 8(5): is the form of my document as required?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) practice directions
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) remotely composed
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- Order 3, Rule 6 in the absence of prescription
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- none: a bare "must" not met
-- Order 28, rule 8(6): is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(6): every condition met, the contrary not proved
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 8(6): deemed until the contrary is proved (O 28 r 1), and it has been
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(6): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(6): condition 2 missing
-- Order 28, rule 8(7)(a): is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority?
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 28 r 8(7)(a): every condition met, the contrary not proved
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 28 r 8(7)(a): deemed until the contrary is proved (O 28 r 1), and it has been
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(7)(a): condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 28 r 8(7)(a): condition 2 missing

-- Order 28, rule 9: Signing of electronic documents
-- Order 28, rule 9(1): is a requirement of signing deemed complied with when my document is filed through an authorised user or registered user?
