-- Order 32 -- Administration and similar actions

-- Order 32, rule 1: Definitions of this Order
-- Order 32, rule 1: is my action an administration action?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is my action an administration action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an action for the administration of an estate
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is my action an administration action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an action for the execution of a trust
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is my action an administration action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means": neither
-- Order 32, rule 1: is this person a personal representative?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is this person a personal representative` `o 32 r 1 an executor` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "includes executors"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is this person a personal representative` `o 32 r 1 an administrator` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "includes administrators"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is this person a personal representative` `o 32 r 1 a trustee` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "includes ... trustees"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 1, is this person a personal representative` `o 32 r 1 any other kind of person` EQUALS NOTHING -- "includes": the list is not closed

-- Order 32, rule 2: Determination of questions, etc., without administration
-- Order 32, rule 2(1): may an action be brought for a question or relief that could be had in an administration action?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(1), may an action be brought for a question or relief that could be had in an administration action` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 32 r 2(1): every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(1), may an action be brought for a question or relief that could be had in an administration action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 32 r 2(1): condition 1 missing
-- Order 32, rule 2(1): must a claim for administration or execution be made in my action?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(1), must a claim for administration or execution be made in my action` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "need not be made"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(1), must a claim for administration or execution be made in my action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an action not under paragraph (1)
-- Order 32, rule 2(2): may an action be brought for the determination of this question?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(2), may an action be brought for the determination of this question` `o 32 r 2(2)(a) a question arising in the administration of the estate of a deceased person or in the execution of a trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(2), may an action be brought for the determination of this question` `o 32 r 2(2)(b) a question as to the composition of a class of persons having a claim against the estate or a beneficial interest in the estate or in property subject to a trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(2), may an action be brought for the determination of this question` `o 32 r 2(2)(c) a question as to the rights or interests of a person claiming to be a creditor of the estate or to be entitled under a will or on the intestacy or to be beneficially entitled under a trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(2), may an action be brought for the determination of this question` `o 32 r 2(2) any other question` EQUALS NOTHING -- "Without limiting paragraph (1)"
-- Order 32, rule 2(3): may an action be brought for this relief?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(3), may an action be brought for this relief` `o 32 r 2(3)(a) an order requiring a personal representative to provide and, if necessary, verify accounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(3), may an action be brought for this relief` `o 32 r 2(3)(b) an order requiring the payment into Court of money held by a person as personal representative` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(3), may an action be brought for this relief` `o 32 r 2(3)(c) an order directing a person to do or abstain from doing a particular act as personal representative` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 2(3), may an action be brought for this relief` `o 32 r 2(3) any other relief` EQUALS NOTHING -- "Without limiting paragraph (1)"

-- Order 32, rule 3: Parties
-- Order 32, rule 3(1): must all the personal representatives be parties to the action?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(1), must all the personal representatives be parties to the action` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 32 r 3(1) all: the duty arises
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(1), must all the personal representatives be parties to the action` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- O 32 r 3(1) all: trigger or exception 1: the duty does not arise
-- Order 32, rule 3(1): are all the personal representatives parties to the action?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(1), are all the personal representatives parties to the action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- O 32 r 3(1) all: every condition met
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(1), are all the personal representatives parties to the action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 32 r 3(1) all: condition 1 missing
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(1), are all the personal representatives parties to the action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- O 32 r 3(1) all: condition 2 missing
-- Order 32, rule 3(2): must every person with a beneficial interest or claim be a party?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(2), must every person with a beneficial interest or claim be a party` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "need not be parties to the action"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(2), must every person with a beneficial interest or claim be a party` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an action outside paragraph (1)
-- Order 32, rule 3(3): is a party other than the executors or administrators entitled to appear on a claim against the estate?
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(3), is a party other than the executors or administrators entitled to appear on a claim against the estate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no permission: "no party other than the executors or administrators ... is entitled to appear"
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(3), is a party other than the executors or administrators entitled to appear on a claim against the estate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- permission given: with the permission the party is entitled to appear (QA)
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(3), is a party other than the executors or administrators entitled to appear on a claim against the estate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the executors themselves: the paragraph is silent
#ASSERT `Under Order 32, rule 3(3), is a party other than the executors or administrators entitled to appear on a claim against the estate` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a claim by a party: the paragraph is silent

-- Order 32, rule 5: Judgments and orders in administration actions
