-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 59 -- cases
-- ===========================================================================

-- Rule 1.  The asker is a private party to a proceeding with the Government.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to my proceeding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to my proceeding` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Government Proceedings Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: the reference names another Act expressly: the Rule is silent.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Government Proceedings Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Government Proceedings Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, which part of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings by or against the Government mean` EQUALS "Part III of the Act"
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, which provision of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings to which the Government is a party mean` EQUALS "Part V of the Act, by virtue of section 2(3)"
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order` `roc11 a judgment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order` `roc11 an award` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order` `roc11 a declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: a thing that is not on the list: "includes" does not close the list.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order` `roc11 something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Case: I hold an order made in civil proceedings against the Government, in my favour.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is the order I hold an order against the Government` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: made in connection with an arbitration.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is the order I hold an order against the Government` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Case: made in neither: a "means" definition says no.
#ASSERT `Under Order 59, rule 1, is the order I hold an order against the Government` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Case: not in favour of a person against the Government.
