-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts, asking about Orders 64 to 70 and the First to Fourth Schedules.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online; it is not the official text.
--
-- Each assertion asks one seat question on stated facts and carries, after `--`, the reason the text gives the expected answer.
-- Every expected answer was decided from the text before the file was run; a failing assertion is a finding, not a value to edit.
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules give; NOTHING is the Rules not answering on those facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- The seat inputs of each question are listed in the order the question declares them.

